Every location contains five individual puzzle chambers followed by one treasure chamber.
The progression must follow this exact structural pattern:
Enter location → Solve puzzle → Collect key → Unlock door → Animate entry into next chamber → Solve next puzzle.
Repeat this process for all five puzzle chambers.
After the fifth puzzle:
Collect fifth key → Unlock final location door → Enter treasure chamber → Reveal treasure → Complete topic → Return to world map.
Each chamber should feel like a physical space inside the location. Use the existing illustrated environment, doors, props, locks, and animations to make the experience tangible.
Door mechanics
Every puzzle chamber must have a visible locked door.
When a player enters a chamber, the environment should communicate that another locked door blocks progress.
The player explores the chamber and interacts with its objects to uncover and solve the puzzle.
